 "debrief": "In Caesar’s account, he sailed along the coast from the cliffs to an open beach, where the Britons met him with cavalry and chariots. The transports grounded in deep water and the soldiers hesitated, until warships with catapults and slingers drove the Britons back and the eagle-bearer of the Tenth leapt into the sea, crying that the men should not betray their eagle. The Romans fought their way ashore, but without cavalry could not pursue. After a storm wrecked many ships, Caesar returned to Gaul before winter. The other choices are what-ifs.",
